  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Kushenol U may be a potential modulator of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2, as it acts as a target of multiple compounds that are themselves targets of the kinase. Specifically, Kushenol U is linked to L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain, which is a target of three different compounds—Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, 3-Epi-29-Acetoxystelliferin E, and Cannabisin D—all of which are associated with the kinase. This indicates that Kushenol U may interact with the kinase through a common downstream pathway, potentially influencing its activity. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible regulatory role of Kushenol U in the kinase pathway, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
